WEBVTT

00:02.894 --> 00:06.332
*

00:07.533 --> 00:10.436
(upbeat theme music playing)

00:10.469 --> 00:17.343
*

00:21.580 --> 00:24.550
Good evening,
and welcome to "Montague."

00:24.583 --> 00:26.818
I'm your host,
Franklin Montague.

00:26.852 --> 00:28.320
And today we're gonna
take a look

00:28.354 --> 00:30.822
at the growing outlook
of accepted sexuality

00:30.856 --> 00:33.225
and its effects
on black youth and culture.

00:33.259 --> 00:34.860
With us today, we have

00:34.893 --> 00:37.629
the Head of the Center
of Trans-American Issues,

00:37.663 --> 00:39.131
Dr. Debra Holt,

00:39.165 --> 00:41.667
and recording artist
Paper Boi.

00:41.700 --> 00:43.302
Good evening to you both.

00:43.335 --> 00:44.703
-Good evening, Montague.
-'Sup?

00:44.736 --> 00:46.305
Uh, let's start
at the beginning.

00:46.338 --> 00:49.375
Paper Boi, last Tuesday
you engaged in a Twitter rant

00:49.408 --> 00:52.211
that had some pretty
inflammatory statements.

00:52.244 --> 00:54.012
But the one statement
that seems to have made

00:54.046 --> 00:55.647
-the biggest impact...
-(sighs)

00:55.681 --> 00:57.683
Was this one and I quote,
"Y'all the..."

00:57.716 --> 01:01.587
N-words "who said I was weird
for not wanting to"

01:01.620 --> 01:03.989
F-word "Caitlyn Jenner."

01:04.022 --> 01:06.825
Would you want to, uh,
explain that statement?

01:06.858 --> 01:08.894
No.

01:10.729 --> 01:14.833
Well, could you
explain that statement?

01:14.866 --> 01:17.169
(blows)
I...

01:17.203 --> 01:18.837
meant what I said.

01:18.870 --> 01:22.208
You don't think
your tweets are transphobic?

01:22.241 --> 01:23.742
I just don't have to
have sex

01:23.775 --> 01:25.244
with Caitlyn Jenner
'cause y'all say so.

01:25.277 --> 01:27.045
Mm.
So you don't think

01:27.079 --> 01:28.780
-Caitlyn Jenner's important?
-(tsks)

01:28.814 --> 01:30.282
Look, I get what
y'all saying, right?

01:30.316 --> 01:33.018
But she's not
super important to me,

01:33.051 --> 01:34.586
like, not my life.

01:34.620 --> 01:38.023
So how long
have you disliked transpeople?

01:38.056 --> 01:40.259
Man, look,
I just found out they exist,

01:40.292 --> 01:41.860
-to be honest.
-I--No, no--

01:41.893 --> 01:43.962
"I make her switch sides,
Caitlyn Jenner in reverse"?

01:43.995 --> 01:45.897
Is that not a--
a lyric of yours?

01:45.931 --> 01:47.433
Man, I was just rapping, man.

01:47.466 --> 01:49.368
Look, I've said worse things.

01:49.401 --> 01:51.703
You ever heard my song,
"Illuminati Sex"?

01:51.737 --> 01:53.305
-Haven't heard it yet.
-Well, there we go then.

01:53.339 --> 01:55.107
Debra, you've written

01:55.141 --> 01:57.309
about this current phenomenon
in your book,

01:57.343 --> 02:00.112
Transition:
Gender in a New Generation.

02:00.146 --> 02:02.381
What do you think
about all this?

02:02.414 --> 02:04.283
I look at these statements as

02:04.316 --> 02:06.252
natural consequences
of a culture

02:06.285 --> 02:08.053
-of exclusion and power.
-Mm.

02:08.086 --> 02:09.555
You know, there's--
there's a large swath of...

02:09.588 --> 02:11.757
-(scoffs)
-Gender and sexuality roles

02:11.790 --> 02:14.726
that are just being exposed to
a large portion of the public.

02:14.760 --> 02:16.295
(chuckling)

02:16.328 --> 02:18.397
DEBRA: Uh, it's harder
for certain sections

02:18.430 --> 02:19.931
to deal with this transition

02:19.965 --> 02:22.168
uh, because of conflict
of interest,

02:22.201 --> 02:24.770
and, frankly, identity issues.

02:24.803 --> 02:26.472
In this case,
the rap community.

02:26.505 --> 02:28.474
Now, I truly believe
it's, uh,

02:28.507 --> 02:30.842
has more to do with issues
of masculinity

02:30.876 --> 02:33.245
in the black community
than actual

02:33.279 --> 02:35.347
homophobia or--or transphobia.

02:35.381 --> 02:37.283
-Please explain.
-Yes, please, please.

02:37.316 --> 02:38.984
Tell me--
tell me about myself.

02:39.017 --> 02:40.586
Go on.

02:40.619 --> 02:43.189
Well, Mis--Mister, uh, Pa--
Mr. Paper Boi--

02:43.222 --> 02:44.490
Mister, yeah.

02:44.523 --> 02:47.092
What would you
consider yourself?

02:47.125 --> 02:48.260
A rapper?

02:48.294 --> 02:49.328
A straight rapper?

02:49.361 --> 02:50.796
Hell yeah.

02:50.829 --> 02:52.464
Well, I did some research
on your lyrics,

02:52.498 --> 02:55.033
and they're actually
very pro sexual-spectrum.

02:55.066 --> 02:56.368
-Oh?
-Pro-what?

02:56.402 --> 02:58.670
"If I eff with you,
you my N-word,

02:58.704 --> 03:00.138
you my N-word for life."

03:00.172 --> 03:01.540
Yo, you know
that ain't what I meant.

03:01.573 --> 03:02.808
Yeah, oh, I understand,
but, you know,

03:02.841 --> 03:04.276
there's a layer of fluidity...

03:04.310 --> 03:05.811
No, no, no.
There's no extra layer.

03:05.844 --> 03:07.679
DEBRA: That you yourself
don't even realize.

03:07.713 --> 03:09.281
I don't think about
what I'm rapping half the time.

03:09.315 --> 03:10.349
Look, I'm just trying
to get paid,

03:10.382 --> 03:11.683
you feel me?
Look, (bleep),

03:11.717 --> 03:13.452
why you think
I'm on this show?

03:13.485 --> 03:16.522
You're not
getting paid for this.

03:16.555 --> 03:18.857
Hey--
Hey, Earn--man?

03:18.890 --> 03:21.493
Black men aren't ready
to accept the implications

03:21.527 --> 03:23.229
of a trans-accepting culture.

03:23.262 --> 03:25.030
No--look, I'm allowed
to say that it's weird.

03:25.063 --> 03:26.532
"It"?

03:26.565 --> 03:27.899
No, look, I'm not
calling him a "it."

03:27.933 --> 03:29.301
-Naw, I'm just saying that--
-"Him"?

03:29.335 --> 03:30.836
Look--look, can I say something?
Damn!

03:30.869 --> 03:32.371
FRANKLIN: All right.
-Well, it depends.

03:32.404 --> 03:34.072
-I was trying to say--
-We got to take a break.

03:34.105 --> 03:35.707
When we're back,
we're gonna take a look

03:35.741 --> 03:38.577
into a young boy's struggle
for equality.

03:38.610 --> 03:39.578
(theme music playing)

03:39.611 --> 03:40.846
(sighs)

03:40.879 --> 03:42.714
(theme music)

03:43.915 --> 03:45.183
(sportscaster on phone)

03:45.217 --> 03:46.385
(front entrance dings)

03:46.418 --> 03:49.255
(Muzak plays in background)

03:49.288 --> 03:53.592
*

03:53.625 --> 03:56.395
(sportscasters continue)

03:56.428 --> 03:57.296
(beep)

04:01.132 --> 04:02.434
$1.49?

04:02.468 --> 04:04.503
But the price
on the can, though.

04:04.536 --> 04:06.037
The price
is on the can, though.

04:06.071 --> 04:08.774
(crowd cheers on phone)

04:08.807 --> 04:11.910
(sportscasters continue)

04:14.880 --> 04:17.849
(jazzy lounge music)

04:17.883 --> 04:24.756
*

04:43.742 --> 04:46.612
(music continues)

04:46.645 --> 04:52.484
*

04:56.288 --> 04:59.325
(upbeat hip-hop instrumental
music)

04:59.358 --> 05:06.264
*

05:18.276 --> 05:19.911
MAN: The Dodge Charger.

05:19.945 --> 05:22.814
Make a statement without
saying anything at all.

05:23.949 --> 05:27.419
(theme music playing)

05:27.453 --> 05:29.120
Earlier in our show,
we talked about

05:29.154 --> 05:30.856
transitions in sexuality.

05:30.889 --> 05:32.658
Uh, but what about race?

05:32.691 --> 05:35.126
Our correspondent,
Nathan Wielder,

05:35.160 --> 05:36.328
has the story.

05:45.303 --> 05:46.872
Harrison looks from the outside

05:46.905 --> 05:48.640
to be your average teenager.

05:48.674 --> 05:51.343
He goes to school,
plays video games,

05:51.377 --> 05:54.045
even listens to music
in his room.

05:54.079 --> 05:55.781
But there's one difference.

05:55.814 --> 05:58.384
I'm a 35-year-old white man.

05:58.417 --> 06:00.819
NATHAN: Harrison,
born Antwoine Smalls,

06:00.852 --> 06:02.788
has trans-racial identity,

06:02.821 --> 06:04.523
identifying as Harrison Booth,

06:04.556 --> 06:07.826
a 35-year-old white man
from Colorado.

06:07.859 --> 06:09.327
And when did you know
that you were a

06:09.361 --> 06:10.962
35-year-old white man?

06:10.996 --> 06:12.498
Well, I've always
felt different.

06:12.531 --> 06:14.900
I go to the store,
the movies,

06:14.933 --> 06:16.468
and just be thinking
to myself, like,

06:16.502 --> 06:19.671
"Why am I not getting
the respect I deserve?"

06:19.705 --> 06:22.841
And then,
it just hit me.

06:22.874 --> 06:24.976
I'm white...

06:25.010 --> 06:26.712
and 35.

06:26.745 --> 06:28.814
I just miss Colorado sometimes,
you know.

06:28.847 --> 06:30.682
Here, I pretend the buildings
are the old

06:30.716 --> 06:33.318
San Juan Mountain ranges but,
you know, the jobs is here.

06:33.351 --> 06:34.753
And where do you work?

06:34.786 --> 06:36.522
I'm a Systems Engineer
for Coca-Cola.

06:36.555 --> 06:37.489
Oh. Okay.

06:37.523 --> 06:38.724
That boy don't work.

06:38.757 --> 06:40.325
He go to school,
and that's it.

06:40.358 --> 06:41.527
-Mm-hmm.
-One day, he said,

06:41.560 --> 06:43.194
"Call me Harrison."

06:43.228 --> 06:45.163
I said, "Who's that?"

06:45.196 --> 06:46.565
He said, "Me."

06:46.598 --> 06:49.067
Do you believe
that he is a white man?

06:49.100 --> 06:50.702
I mean, he isn't.

06:50.736 --> 06:52.571
(bleep), I'd love
to wake up one day and say,

06:52.604 --> 06:54.773
"Hey, everybody,
I'm Rihanna."

06:54.806 --> 06:55.774
But I ain't.

06:55.807 --> 06:56.775
It's been pretty hard.

06:56.808 --> 06:58.610
My family just doesn't get it.

06:58.644 --> 07:00.846
You know, I try to get them
to go out with me,

07:00.879 --> 07:03.014
go on walks,
go to the farmers market,

07:03.048 --> 07:05.884
chat with people,
but...yeah.

07:05.917 --> 07:08.720
So why don't you think
that they get it?

07:08.754 --> 07:10.456
I don't think
they get it because

07:10.489 --> 07:12.791
they don't realize that race
is just a made-up thing.

07:12.824 --> 07:14.025
Mm-hmm.

07:14.059 --> 07:15.360
They grew up
having labels, and me,

07:15.393 --> 07:16.762
I'm just--I'm just
not like that.

07:16.795 --> 07:18.096
I see.

07:18.129 --> 07:20.432
So how do you embrace
your identity?

07:20.466 --> 07:21.933
-I dress a certain way.
-Ah.

07:21.967 --> 07:23.134
Patagonia.

07:23.168 --> 07:25.070
I wear a thick,
brown leather belt.

07:25.103 --> 07:27.372
I like to envision myself
after the surgery.

07:27.405 --> 07:28.874
(clears throat)

07:28.907 --> 07:32.277
"Hey, excuse me,
what IPA do you have on tap?"

07:32.310 --> 07:36.548
"Hey, did you see
Game of Thrones last night?"

07:36.582 --> 07:38.049
Yeah.

07:38.083 --> 07:39.751
So your--
your surgery,

07:39.785 --> 07:40.919
that's later this year?

07:40.952 --> 07:42.253
Right.
I started working

07:42.287 --> 07:43.989
at Stonecrest Mall,
so hopefully

07:44.022 --> 07:46.091
by then I have enough money
to take the next step.

07:46.124 --> 07:47.459
Mm-hmm.

07:47.493 --> 07:50.829
So you work at Coca-Cola
and the mall?

07:50.862 --> 07:54.132
Right.
Correct, I work at both.

07:54.165 --> 07:55.934
NATHAN: Harrison
has been planning

07:55.967 --> 07:58.737
a full racial transition
with a Dr. Samuel Vergara

07:58.770 --> 08:00.572
who guarantees Harrison
can visually transition

08:00.606 --> 08:02.407
through an experimental
procedure

08:02.440 --> 08:04.743
that will allow Harrison
not only to be a white man

08:04.776 --> 08:06.311
but whatever race he chooses.

08:06.344 --> 08:10.315
The procedure's
absolutely 100% possible.

08:10.348 --> 08:12.618
He's gonna look weird though.

08:12.651 --> 08:14.419
NATHAN: But before Harrison
can fully realize

08:14.452 --> 08:17.122
his physical identity,
he still has the day-to-day

08:17.155 --> 08:19.825
that's filled with
discrimination and ridicule.

08:19.858 --> 08:21.292
It--it's pretty awful,
you know.

08:21.326 --> 08:22.994
You--you walk
in the streets,

08:23.028 --> 08:25.196
and black people, they see you,
they nod to you like,

08:25.230 --> 08:26.965
"Hey, good to see us."

08:26.998 --> 08:29.200
And it's to the point
where I've just given up.

08:29.234 --> 08:30.936
I've stopped trying
to convince them

08:30.969 --> 08:33.672
-that I'm not "us."
-Gotcha.

08:33.705 --> 08:36.007
Hey, excuse me,
this is definitely the guy.

08:36.041 --> 08:38.043
He doesn't even live
in the area.

08:38.076 --> 08:39.678
I've never seen him before.

08:44.082 --> 08:47.052
(police radio chatter)

08:47.085 --> 08:48.987
*

08:49.020 --> 08:51.122
HARRISON: I think
we're taking slow strides,

08:51.156 --> 08:53.224
but you have to believe
things are getting better,

08:53.258 --> 08:55.360
otherwise,
you'll just die inside.

08:55.393 --> 08:57.062
Is there anything
you'd like to say to

08:57.095 --> 08:59.164
other black kids out there
who may be going through

08:59.197 --> 09:00.866
the same thing?

09:00.899 --> 09:02.167
Just be you.

09:02.200 --> 09:04.002
At all costs.

09:04.035 --> 09:05.671
But also,

09:05.704 --> 09:08.239
stop dressing so crazy.

09:08.273 --> 09:09.708
Hmm.

09:09.741 --> 09:12.711
(gentle instrumental music)

09:12.744 --> 09:19.618
*

09:23.722 --> 09:26.658
(guitar music flourishes)

09:26.692 --> 09:28.259
Absolutely.

09:29.427 --> 09:31.029
Hi.

09:31.062 --> 09:33.364
I'm Devyonne Johnson,
famous movie star.

09:33.398 --> 09:36.034
When the director calls cut
and I get a quick five,

09:36.067 --> 09:38.503
you know I'm reaching
for the smooth taste

09:38.536 --> 09:40.438
of Swisher Sweets.

09:40.471 --> 09:43.208
Swisher Sweets are the only
cigarillos made with

09:43.241 --> 09:46.745
the highest quality tobacco
from family-owned farms.

09:46.778 --> 09:48.747
It's their high standards
and experience

09:48.780 --> 09:52.250
that make for a quality smoke
you can enjoy every time.

09:53.551 --> 09:54.886
(sniffs)

09:57.222 --> 09:58.189
(click)

09:58.223 --> 10:04.930
*

10:06.431 --> 10:09.635
(blows)

10:09.668 --> 10:11.302
Yeah...
(chuckles)

10:13.104 --> 10:14.806
I only smoke Swisher Sweets.

10:16.507 --> 10:18.109
It's the smooth taste.

10:20.245 --> 10:23.414
These Swisher Sweets
is good as hell.

10:23.448 --> 10:26.952
Here, make sure
this one's empty.

10:26.985 --> 10:28.419
Swisher Sweets.

10:28.453 --> 10:29.988
There's just
something about 'em.

10:30.021 --> 10:32.924
And try our new pre-dumps
Swisher Sweets as well.

10:39.765 --> 10:42.734
(mellow jazz music)

10:42.768 --> 10:46.672
*

10:47.806 --> 10:51.109
(theme music playing)

10:51.142 --> 10:53.144
And we're back.
And today we're talking about

10:53.178 --> 10:55.013
transitions with my guests,

10:55.046 --> 10:58.483
Atlanta rapper Paper Boi
and Dr. Debra Holt.

10:58.516 --> 11:01.586
Ah, Paper Boi, are you afraid
to speak your mind

11:01.619 --> 11:03.188
on this subject?

11:03.221 --> 11:05.657
Actually, yup, I am.

11:05.691 --> 11:07.693
You can't say real (bleep)
anymore without somebody

11:07.726 --> 11:09.928
trying to make sure
you never make money forever.

11:09.961 --> 11:11.329
FRANKLIN: So you think
you're being persecuted?

11:11.362 --> 11:12.998
Yes, I am.

11:13.031 --> 11:14.700
Man, you can't even say
"ho" in a song no more.

11:14.733 --> 11:16.367
(scoffs)
A travesty, I'm sure.

11:16.401 --> 11:17.635
-(chuckles)
ALFRED: Yo, why you--

11:17.669 --> 11:19.170
Yo, why you talk
like that?

11:19.204 --> 11:20.672
Like, "a travesty, I'm sur--"
like, what?

11:20.706 --> 11:22.640
You're--you're whining
about chickens

11:22.674 --> 11:24.042
-coming home to roost.
-No-no-no-no-no.

11:24.075 --> 11:25.944
Rap is chickens
coming home to roost.

11:25.977 --> 11:28.646
Look, my life is messed up
from (bleep) y'all did, okay?

11:28.680 --> 11:30.215
That's black news.
You can look that up.

11:30.248 --> 11:31.950
Well, your news
is problematic.

11:31.983 --> 11:33.785
-Bitch, that ain't my fault!
-Whoa, whoa, whoa!

11:33.819 --> 11:35.386
I won't have you on my show
calling anyone "bitches."

11:35.420 --> 11:36.788
How you gonna blame me
for news being bad, huh?

11:36.822 --> 11:38.289
FRANKLIN: All right,
simmer down, simmer down.

11:38.323 --> 11:39.691
You can't even have
an intelligent dialogue

11:39.725 --> 11:41.492
-without spewing profanities.
-(groans)

11:41.526 --> 11:42.894
-It's--it's ludicrous.
FRANKLIN: Okay, okay, okay.

11:42.928 --> 11:45.997
Paper Boi,
isn't a lack of a father

11:46.031 --> 11:48.166
the reason you hate transpeople?

11:48.199 --> 11:49.567
What?
Lack of a father?

11:49.600 --> 11:51.369
Man, you hear yourself?
(bleep), shut up.

11:51.402 --> 11:52.670
Man, here's the thing.

11:52.704 --> 11:54.405
Man, I--
it's hard for me to care

11:54.439 --> 11:56.174
about this when nobody
cares about me

11:56.207 --> 11:57.976
as a black human man,
you feel me?

11:58.009 --> 11:59.745
Like, Caitlyn Jenner
is just doing

11:59.778 --> 12:01.379
what rich white men been doing
since the dawn of time,

12:01.412 --> 12:03.014
which is whatever
the hell he want.

12:03.048 --> 12:05.683
So why should I care?
What make him so special?

12:05.717 --> 12:07.385
But--but as a black man
in this country,

12:07.418 --> 12:09.554
shouldn't you care about
the civil liberties of others,

12:09.587 --> 12:11.022
since they're
so closely related to--to

12:11.056 --> 12:12.423
your struggle for equality?

12:12.457 --> 12:14.225
What you talking 'bout?
I do care.

12:14.259 --> 12:16.161
Look, I don't have a problem
with gay people, transpeople,

12:16.194 --> 12:17.829
because that's tolerance,
but where's tolerance

12:17.863 --> 12:20.231
for people like me?
You know what I'm saying?

12:20.265 --> 12:23.668
Like...
(sighs) Look.

12:23.701 --> 12:25.570
I should be able
to say something is weird

12:25.603 --> 12:27.438
without people hating on me.
All right?

12:27.472 --> 12:30.241
Look, I never--
I never said anything

12:30.275 --> 12:31.676
about taking away
nobody's rights.

12:31.709 --> 12:32.944
A'ight? Never.

12:32.978 --> 12:34.412
I--I understand
what you're saying,

12:34.445 --> 12:36.782
but--but some people
found your remarks offensive.

12:36.815 --> 12:39.751
Yeah, well,
freedom of speech, (bleep).

12:40.986 --> 12:43.388
No, you're right.

12:43.421 --> 12:44.923
I agree.

12:49.961 --> 12:54.065
But your music is detrimental
to black teens.

12:54.099 --> 12:57.268
(scoffs) Yeah, but so is
all rap music, right?

12:57.302 --> 12:58.569
-I mean, and rock music...
-Rock.

12:58.603 --> 12:59.905
Before it was
taken over by rap.

12:59.938 --> 13:01.940
Yeah, I agree.

13:01.973 --> 13:04.742
You hate... women!

13:04.776 --> 13:05.911
(bleep), what?

13:05.944 --> 13:10.115
(theme music playing)

13:10.148 --> 13:12.150
Questions.

13:12.183 --> 13:14.119
The universe.

13:14.152 --> 13:16.421
Paternity tests?

13:16.454 --> 13:17.923
Salutations.

13:17.956 --> 13:19.557
(gentle music)

13:19.590 --> 13:21.960
Hi.
My name is Ahmad White.

13:21.993 --> 13:24.095
You may know me
from your dreams.

13:24.129 --> 13:25.463
Call this number below

13:25.496 --> 13:27.799
and get the answers
you deserve.

13:27.833 --> 13:28.934
(upbeat music)

13:28.967 --> 13:30.435
When I called Ahmad White,

13:30.468 --> 13:32.570
I was three months behind
on my car note.

13:32.603 --> 13:34.806
(scoffs) My stepson,
he was in jail.

13:34.840 --> 13:37.843
My life was in shambles!

13:37.876 --> 13:39.477
But now, I got a truck,

13:39.510 --> 13:42.247
I got a girlfriend,

13:42.280 --> 13:44.615
I got the answers I deserve.

13:44.649 --> 13:46.918
Thank you, Ahmad White.

13:46.952 --> 13:48.419
Most people don't realize

13:48.453 --> 13:51.189
their chakra's
in another universe.

13:51.222 --> 13:52.924
Don't be dumb.

13:52.958 --> 13:54.525
Call now.

13:54.559 --> 13:57.595
Me and Ahmad found out
I was a moon sign,

13:57.628 --> 14:00.098
and I wasn't getting enough
crystal in my diet.

14:00.131 --> 14:03.101
Now, I live
in a beautiful home.

14:03.134 --> 14:05.370
Ahmad gave me the answers
I was looking for.

14:05.403 --> 14:06.838
Come to our Liberty Center

14:06.872 --> 14:09.540
and get a free juice
and Nutella sandwich.

14:09.574 --> 14:12.844
When I called Ahmad,
my life was going nowhere fast.

14:12.878 --> 14:15.046
After a Nutella sandwich
and juice,

14:15.080 --> 14:17.048
my life's a lot better.

14:17.082 --> 14:20.218
(upbeat tone sustained)

14:20.251 --> 14:21.552
Open your third eye.

14:21.586 --> 14:23.188
He works.

14:23.221 --> 14:24.722
He just works.

14:24.755 --> 14:27.893
He works.
He really works.

14:27.926 --> 14:30.295
He works.
He really, really works.

14:30.328 --> 14:32.697
Knowledge is the path
to greatness.

14:32.730 --> 14:35.533
If you'd like to be
smart as a baby dolphin,

14:35.566 --> 14:37.168
call now.

14:37.202 --> 14:40.071
(ethereal music)

14:43.274 --> 14:46.244
(upbeat hip-hop instrumental
music)

14:46.277 --> 14:48.246
*

14:48.279 --> 14:49.948
(engine revs)

14:55.620 --> 14:57.155
That's a nice car.

14:57.188 --> 14:58.756
You know him?

14:58.789 --> 15:00.858
That's Victor Wallace.

15:00.892 --> 15:03.394
His wife left him
for his brother.

15:03.428 --> 15:05.396
Long court battle.

15:05.430 --> 15:07.665
Kids, house--

15:07.698 --> 15:10.068
It got messy.

15:10.101 --> 15:13.071
He ain't say one word
the whole trial.

15:13.104 --> 15:15.606
But then at the end,
he just stood up and said,

15:15.640 --> 15:18.609
"Leave me my Dodge Charger."

15:22.080 --> 15:24.415
He been driving around
this neighborhood

15:24.449 --> 15:26.284
in circles for a week.

15:26.317 --> 15:29.754
-Just waving.
-Mm.

15:29.787 --> 15:31.889
Nice car though.

15:31.923 --> 15:33.291
(nozzle fumbling)

15:33.324 --> 15:36.294
(upbeat hip-hop instrumental
music)

15:36.327 --> 15:41.632
*

15:41.666 --> 15:42.968
(tires screech)

15:43.001 --> 15:44.569
*

15:44.602 --> 15:47.772
MAN: The Dodge Charger.
Keep it in the divorce.

15:49.907 --> 15:52.277
(gasps)
King Coco's Crunch-O's.

15:52.310 --> 15:54.612
The legend is true!

15:54.645 --> 15:55.646
(creaking)

15:55.680 --> 15:57.482
Gimme that crunch!

15:57.515 --> 15:58.950
No!

15:58.984 --> 15:59.951
(grunts)

15:59.985 --> 16:01.219
Nice try.

16:01.252 --> 16:02.287
But only kids can have...

16:02.320 --> 16:04.489
all: Coconut Crunch-O's.

16:04.522 --> 16:06.624
WOLF: That chocolatey
coconut crunch

16:06.657 --> 16:08.459
in every bite.
(crunches)

16:08.493 --> 16:10.661
Oh, I can almost taste it!

16:10.695 --> 16:12.163
Bbbbbb!

16:12.197 --> 16:13.431
(train horn whistles)

16:13.464 --> 16:15.833
Oh, I got to have
them Crunch-O's!

16:15.866 --> 16:17.168
-(grunts)
-Ow! Ow!

16:17.202 --> 16:18.936
Man!
Ow!

16:18.970 --> 16:21.139
-Stop resisting.
-(pained groans)

16:21.172 --> 16:23.074
-Stop resisting, sir.
-(pained struggle) Damn!

16:23.108 --> 16:25.110
-Stop...resisting.
-Shit, man!

16:25.143 --> 16:27.245
Oh! Mother--
(grunts)

16:27.278 --> 16:28.446
Stay down.
(handcuffs click)

16:28.479 --> 16:29.647
What happened?

16:29.680 --> 16:30.848
He's going to jail.

16:30.881 --> 16:31.949
That's what happened.

16:31.983 --> 16:33.784
This is some bullshit!

16:33.818 --> 16:34.819
You all right?

16:34.852 --> 16:36.121
He's fine.

16:36.154 --> 16:38.089
He just doesn't wanna
go to jail.

16:38.123 --> 16:39.357
You sitting on my back, man!

16:39.390 --> 16:40.358
(bones crack)
Ah!

16:40.391 --> 16:41.626
Sir, be quiet.

16:41.659 --> 16:43.261
Yo!
You sitting on his back!

16:43.294 --> 16:45.130
He was trying
to steal your cereal, right?

16:45.163 --> 16:46.998
I mean,
it's just cereal.

16:47.032 --> 16:48.133
He can have it!

16:48.166 --> 16:50.101
Man, I'm just hungry, man!

16:50.135 --> 16:52.103
They don't let wolves
in stores, man!

16:52.137 --> 16:53.504
Step back, guys.

16:53.538 --> 16:54.972
I'm going to
lift the offender up.

16:55.006 --> 16:57.342
We are now going
to our feet, sir.

16:57.375 --> 16:59.110
Let's go, sir, let's go.

16:59.144 --> 17:01.179
Nigga, I could be
eating these kids!

17:01.212 --> 17:03.114
But I'm out here
eating cereal!

17:03.148 --> 17:04.482
Hey, it's cool!

17:04.515 --> 17:06.217
We'll just give him
the cereal.

17:06.251 --> 17:07.618
No, only kids

17:07.652 --> 17:09.954
can have Coconut Crunch-O's.
You know that.

17:09.987 --> 17:11.522
(tsks)
That's a wack law.

17:11.556 --> 17:14.225
This fool know he eat
Coconut Crunch-O's,

17:14.259 --> 17:16.161
and you ain't no kid!

17:16.194 --> 17:18.296
Let me do my job.

17:18.329 --> 17:21.132
I said back up...sir!

17:21.166 --> 17:25.403
(brooding dramatic music)

17:25.436 --> 17:27.905
(crunches)

17:30.375 --> 17:31.842
MAN: Coconut Crunch-O's

17:31.876 --> 17:33.978
is a part of
this balanced breakfast.

17:34.011 --> 17:37.715
(theme music playing)

17:37.748 --> 17:40.385
Earlier we showed a clip
about a young man

17:40.418 --> 17:43.321
dealing with trans-racial
identity.

17:43.354 --> 17:46.857
Well, we've got him joining us
via Facebook video chat.

17:46.891 --> 17:49.560
Please welcome
Antwoine Smalls to the show.

17:49.594 --> 17:52.430
Hello, Montague, thank you
for having me on your show.

17:52.463 --> 17:54.165
-So now, Antwoine...
ALFRED: (laughs)

17:54.199 --> 17:56.767
-It's Harrison.
-I'm sorry.

17:56.801 --> 17:59.070
-Harrison.
-(chuckling)

17:59.104 --> 18:01.406
FRANKLIN: How's your life been
since we last saw you?

18:01.439 --> 18:02.507
ALFRED: Ohh...

18:02.540 --> 18:03.941
It's pretty good.

18:03.974 --> 18:06.111
I just came back
from Charleston, South Carolina.

18:06.144 --> 18:07.712
FRANKLIN: Ah.
-Beautiful.

18:07.745 --> 18:09.280
I was checking out
some cheap art spaces

18:09.314 --> 18:11.048
for me and a friend
that I made, uh--

18:11.082 --> 18:12.683
What--wait--
I'm sorry, I'm sorry, I'm sorry.

18:12.717 --> 18:14.885
Yo. This is dumb.

18:14.919 --> 18:16.754
-Like, that--this is dumb.
DEBRA: What--

18:16.787 --> 18:18.556
ALFRED: Like, dude, wait, wait.
Did you power up?

18:18.589 --> 18:20.225
'Cause you look like
Super Saiyan right now.

18:20.258 --> 18:22.026
Like, is that, like,
is that the Goku...

18:22.059 --> 18:23.261
FRANKLIN: (sighs)
-Like Dragon Ball collection,

18:23.294 --> 18:24.862
my (bleep), like?
You look like

18:24.895 --> 18:26.364
-a fake Ellen DeGeneres.
-This is just...

18:26.397 --> 18:28.199
-Like a Felon DeGeneres.
-Okay.

18:28.233 --> 18:30.968
Look, no-no-no, you look
like Drake Malfoy, dude, like.

18:31.001 --> 18:33.471
Bangs, my (bleep)?
Like, nobody told you

18:33.504 --> 18:35.140
-not to do bangs--Like--
FRANKLIN: Okay, okay.

18:35.173 --> 18:37.275
-Nice tolerance.
FRANKLIN: Mr. Boi.

18:37.308 --> 18:38.943
ALFRED: What is up--Wait, wait--
-Okay, okay, thank you.

18:38.976 --> 18:40.745
-None of y'all? Okay.
FRANKLIN: Thank you.

18:40.778 --> 18:42.079
-That is very inappropriate.
-Sorry, man, go ahead.

18:42.113 --> 18:43.914
-Shh.
-It's--it's okay.

18:43.948 --> 18:46.451
Sadly, the black community,
they just aren't accepting

18:46.484 --> 18:48.085
of racial diversity or

18:48.119 --> 18:49.620
anyone different,
for that matter.

18:49.654 --> 18:51.956
-Mm. Now, Harrison...
ALFRED: (groans)

18:51.989 --> 18:53.991
Would you say that, uh,
the--the rap game

18:54.024 --> 18:56.627
or the hip-hop community
is especially intolerant

18:56.661 --> 18:58.563
of the lifestyle you chose?

18:58.596 --> 19:00.998
We really can't blame rap
or the hip-hop culture.

19:01.031 --> 19:03.734
He's just expressing himself
to the best of his ability.

19:03.768 --> 19:06.070
And I will defend
his right to do that.

19:06.103 --> 19:08.606
He's telling a story, or, like,
views from the streets.

19:08.639 --> 19:10.241
-You know, like a ghetto news.
-Mm.

19:10.275 --> 19:12.109
-Okay. (snickers)
-But--but Harrison,

19:12.143 --> 19:14.345
don't you think
that the rap community

19:14.379 --> 19:17.081
and its treatment of transpeople
and homosexuals

19:17.114 --> 19:20.151
is indicative of a larger
problem in the black community,

19:20.185 --> 19:22.787
one that makes
your lifestyle unacceptable?

19:22.820 --> 19:24.455
No, no way.
Not at all.

19:24.489 --> 19:27.458
I mean, a man wanting
to turn himself into a woman--

19:27.492 --> 19:29.427
that's just unnatural,
and I don't think

19:29.460 --> 19:32.263
we should have our kids
thinking that that's okay.

19:32.297 --> 19:33.831
So I will support that message.

19:33.864 --> 19:35.333
Wait, wait, wait, wait.

19:35.366 --> 19:36.601
-What are you saying?
-(stifled laugh)

19:36.634 --> 19:38.102
I'm not into gay marriage.

19:38.135 --> 19:39.637
That--that is gross.

19:39.670 --> 19:41.172
Why would I ever tolerate
something like that?

19:41.206 --> 19:42.607
Marriage is meant for

19:42.640 --> 19:44.209
a man and a woman,
not that--

19:44.242 --> 19:46.311
that's an abomination.
We're--We--No.

19:46.344 --> 19:47.978
How can you say that

19:48.012 --> 19:49.714
with the discrimination
you were just talking about?

19:49.747 --> 19:51.282
-I mean, how--
-It's the truth.

19:51.316 --> 19:53.951
-What are you, crazy?
-This (bleep) crazy!

19:53.984 --> 19:55.620
That is all the time
we have tonight.

19:55.653 --> 19:57.388
-I'd like to thank my guests...
ALFRED: Oh, my God.

19:57.422 --> 19:59.524
-Dr. Holt, Paper Boi.
ALFRED: (chuckling)

19:59.557 --> 20:02.327
Please check for her book
Transition,

20:02.360 --> 20:05.029
as well as
Paper Boi's mixtape Postal.

20:05.062 --> 20:06.831
ALFRED: Yup!
-Available...

20:06.864 --> 20:09.834
wherever mixtapes
are available.

20:09.867 --> 20:12.403
-Good night.
ALFRED: (laughing)

20:12.437 --> 20:15.673
Like, you look
like a dying palm tree.

20:15.706 --> 20:18.376
Right? Like you look like
the lost fifth Beatle,

20:18.409 --> 20:20.144
my (bleep), that they just
don't talk about.

20:20.177 --> 20:22.247
That, like, power up,
like--

20:22.280 --> 20:24.849
they gave him (bleep) bangs,
like--(laughing).

20:24.882 --> 20:26.517
DEBRA: I don't care for it.

20:26.551 --> 20:29.520
(theme music playing)

20:29.554 --> 20:36.394
*

21:24.909 --> 21:26.777
(dramatic music)

21:28.112 --> 21:29.980
(low sustained tone)
